---
import '../design/design-aids.css';
import SketchSheet from '../design/SketchSheet.astro';
---
<transaction-recovery-lab class="lab design-aid design-lab" aria-labelledby="transaction-recovery-title">
  <div class="lab-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Interactive experiment</span></div>
  <h3 id="transaction-recovery-title">One missing reply, two possible histories</h3>
  <div class="lab-introduction"><p>Ada intends to buy two mugs. Five are available, so an accidental second purchase could succeed too. K14 identifies her original intent. Compare what actually happened inside the database with what the application knows.</p><p class="try-this">Step through a committed purchase whose reply is lost. Try recovering with the same key, then with a new key. Finally change the hidden history to a rollback: the application receives the same missing answer.</p></div>
  <div class="lab-controls" data-controls>
    <p class="lab-area-label">Controls</p>
    <div class="control-line"><label for="transaction-recovery-ending">What actually happened</label><select id="transaction-recovery-ending" data-ending><option value="commit">Commit succeeded; reply was lost</option><option value="rollback">Commit never took effect; transaction rolled back</option></select></div>
    <div class="control-line"><label for="transaction-recovery-key">Recovery choice</label><select id="transaction-recovery-key" data-key><option value="same">Keep K14: same intent</option><option value="new">Create K15: mistaken new identity</option></select></div>
    <div class="control-line"><button type="button" data-back>Previous step</button><button type="button" data-next>Next step</button><button type="button" data-reset>Start again</button></div>
  </div>
  <div class="lab-output paper-surface">
    <p class="lab-area-label">Result <span data-step>Starting state</span></p>
    <div class="recovery-counts"><span>Committed mugs available</span><strong data-stock>5</strong><span>Committed orders for this intent</span><strong data-orders>0</strong></div>
    <div class="recovery-sides"><SketchSheet tone="teal"><h4>Database reality</h4><p data-database>5 mugs available; no order for K14.</p></SketchSheet><SketchSheet tone="amber"><h4>Application’s knowledge and action</h4><p data-application>Retains K14: Ada wants 2 mugs at €20 each.</p></SketchSheet></div>
    <p class="recovery-event" data-event role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">This experiment starts with five mugs so an accidental second purchase can also succeed.</p>
  </div>
  <details class="model-note"><summary>What this experiment models</summary><p>This is a fixed teaching schedule, not a live database or network. The original transaction ends before recovery begins. Both histories lose the commit answer; only the reader can see the selected hidden outcome. Recovery uses a unique key on the order, verifies matching purchase details, and changes stock only in the successful new-claim branch. Availability and order counters show committed state. Other buyers, key expiry and database state loss are outside the model. If the original transaction is still active, a repeated claim may wait for it instead.</p></details>
  <noscript><p>If the original purchase committed, retaining K14 recovers one order while inventing K15 can create two. If the original purchase rolled back, either key can create one order. The application cannot choose a safe policy by assuming which hidden history occurred.</p></noscript>
</transaction-recovery-lab>
<script>
  import { recoveryState } from './transaction-recovery-model.mjs';
  class TransactionRecoveryLab extends HTMLElement {
    connectedCallback() {
      if (this.dataset.ready) return;
      const ending = this.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-ending]')!;
      const key = this.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-key]')!;
      const back = this.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-back]')!;
      const next = this.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-next]')!;
      let step = 0;
      const render = () => {
        const state = recoveryState(step, ending.value === 'commit', key.value === 'same');
        for (const name of ['stock', 'orders', 'database', 'application', 'event'] as const) {
          this.querySelector(`[data-${name}]`)!.textContent = String(state[name]);
        }
        this.querySelector('[data-step]')!.textContent = `Step ${step} of 5`;
        back.disabled = step === 0; next.disabled = step === 5;
      };
      const reset = () => { step = 0; render(); };
      back.addEventListener('click', () => { step = Math.max(0, step - 1); render(); });
      next.addEventListener('click', () => { step = Math.min(5, step + 1); render(); });
      this.querySelector('[data-reset]')!.addEventListener('click', reset);
      ending.addEventListener('change', reset); key.addEventListener('change', reset);
      render(); this.dataset.ready = 'true';
    }
  }
  if (!customElements.get('transaction-recovery-lab')) customElements.define('transaction-recovery-lab', TransactionRecoveryLab);
</script>
<style>
  .recovery-counts { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) auto; gap:.65rem 1rem; border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule); padding-bottom:1rem; margin-bottom:1.2rem; font:.85rem/1.5 var(--font-sans); }
  .recovery-counts strong { font:500 1.3rem/1.2 var(--font-mono); }
  .recovery-sides { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:1rem; }
  .recovery-sides p { font:.9rem/1.65 var(--font-sans); margin:.6rem 0 0; }
  .recovery-event { border-left:2px solid var(--teal); padding-left:.9rem; font:.875rem/1.7 var(--font-sans); margin:1.3rem 0 .3rem; }
  @media(max-width:560px) { .recovery-sides { grid-template-columns:1fr; } }
</style>
